      "content": "# Electrotechnology NQF Level 2 November 2025 Examination Paper - source capture\n\nNotebook: https://notebook.google.com/notebook/625ae2a2-3198-4f9e-b906-dbd9915ca3a9\nCaptured: 2026-09-30T21:03:04.635Z | walker: notebooklm-ingestion extension | sources: 1/1 | text chars: 0 | page images: 6 | summaries: 1\nProvenance: research/captures/notebooklm_sources/07_Electrotechnology_NQF_Level_2_November_2025_Examination_Paper_625ae2a2.json sha256 1DD1FBB1F0ABD176870A660C385B7F941DC6838D44D646575BAAEA9905F68E4E\n\n## 1. Electrotechnology NQF Level 2 - November 2025 - Y-Paper.pdf\n\nType: pdf | text chars: 0 | page images: 6 | summary chars: 837\n\n### Summary\n\nThis document is a formal **National Certificate (Vocational) examination paper** for **Electrotechnology NQF Level 2**, issued by the South African Department of Higher Education and Training. The assessment evaluates a student's grasp of **fundamental electrical principles**, including Ohm’s law, circuit analysis, and the identification of **IEC symbols** used in technical diagrams. Beyond theoretical physics, the paper emphasizes **practical vocational skills** such as the correct application of hand tools, wiring requirements for domestic installations, and the systematic **troubleshooting of electrical faults**. The structure concludes with a **formula sheet** and a simulated **maintenance record**, ensuring that candidates can effectively bridge the gap between classroom calculations and real-world industrial reporting.\n\n### Pages\n\nPDF rendered as 6 page image(s); source text is not exposed in the DOM.\n\n- https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/notebooklm/ABzcPv1w8vgqVMpazDfba9Y3l_vJoDd5LQYwiAGou7ry7ebXtmBENmLdMkKhSIeeVDiPl2ta3C3BcEfTraBcfBLn2HHwlQ_DJ13k7NdXrUKCaFbNqU-IHm2Qa9KyTBRBFELIE_mZ96DRCw=w1410-h971-v0?authuser=0\n- https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/notebooklm/ABzcPv3xN7NR15YzzGMnTZxrygJFfM-KZQuLe2ScESWDNczuYjjWUgJXSF_DAWu_xB5z7yHTYk8JdfCkbP8dKGJ7jlbw4g5fu7xU_US_CZ8F-MmaDu76xYcmqosA69r