      "content": "# Electrotechnology NQF Level 2 November 2025 Examination Paper - Gemini Notebook\n\nSource: https://notebook.google.com/notebook/625ae2a2-3198-4f9e-b906-dbd9915ca3a9\nFetched: 2026-09-30T17:58:05.568Z\nAuth: authenticated CDP session (Edge, debug port 9222)\n\n---\n\nlink_2\nShared\nadd_2\nshare_1\nmore_vert\nsettings\nPRO\nSources\nChat\nStudio\nlandscape_2\n⚡\nElectrotechnology NQF Level 2 November 2025 Examination Paper\n1 source\n·\n23 Feb 2026\n\nThis document presents an Electrotechnology NQF Level 2 examination paper administered by the South African Department of Higher Education and Training on November 21, 2025. The three-hour assessment is worth 100 marks and is designed to test vocational students on fundamental electrical principles, circuit diagrams, and mathematical calculations. It includes five main questions covering true-or-false statements, schematic symbols, electrical block diagrams, multiple-choice theory, and practical fault-finding scenarios. Additionally, the examination package provides a comprehensive formula sheet with thirty-one mathematical equations alongside an addendum for recording maintenance work reports.\n\nkeep_pin\nSave to note\ncopy\nthumb_up\nthumb_down\nHow do electrical components and symbols differ in domestic installations?\nsubdirectory_arrow_right\nWhat tools and safety procedures are essential for electrical maintenance?\nsubdirectory_arrow_right\nExplain the core principles of Ohm's law and circuit calculations.\nsubdirectory_arrow_right\n1 source\narrow_upward\nGemini Notebook can make mistakes, so double-check it.\n\n## Sources (1)\n\n- Electrotechnology NQF Level 2 - November 2025 - Y-Paper.pdf\n\n"
