\nMechatronic systems rely heavily on **remote control operators** to oversee industrial processes safely from a distance, utilizing **low safety voltages** and **intrinsic safety zones** to prevent accidental shocks or explosions. To protect personnel from severe physical harm around automated machinery, mandatory **physical barriers and machine guards** serve as a crucial initial defense. The operational backbone of these setups involves various **proximity sensors and detection switches** that gather environmental data, feeding information into **programmable logic controllers** to coordinate automated actions. Ultimately, these automated networks integrate **relays, solenoids, and mechanical drives** to smoothly execute complex tasks while keeping operators fully informed through distinct **visual and auditory feedback signals**.\n\n### Text\n\nMechatronic Systems L2\nTopic two\nRemote control refers to control occurs over a distance between sites\nRemote control is when the operator sits and monitors and manages the processes a distance away from the actual work area.\nFOUR types of control used in mechatronic systems.\nHardwired control (relay ladder logic)\nElectronic control\nEmbedded control\nProcessor control (PLC/PC)\nIn mechatronics a control panel must work on safety voltages & with intrinsic safety\nSafety voltage refers to a voltage that is considered to be a low voltage (1–50V) that will not shock a person under normal conditions is used in control circuits.\nIntrinsic safety is the region where a flash over arc will not cause a fire or explosion in an area where chemicals are used.\n. Relay logic circuits are represented by various logic operator symbols, such\nas NOT, AND, OR and SR latch functions\n. The symbol of the AND logic operator\nThe related circuit of an AND function using lamp(s) and\nswitching symbols\nIt necessary to have a machine guard on moving machinery\nMachine guards are one’s first line of defence against injuries such as amputations, fractures, lacerations or crushing injuries. OSHA regulations require guarding anywhere where there is a danger of having any body part come in contact with a moving part.\nThe PLC as it conforms to the input-process-output approach\nThe purpose of the temperature sensor as an input to this system, is used to turn the fan on or off when there is a change in the set temperature.\nThe purpose of the start push button as an input to this system is used to start the PLC system.\nThe purpose of the stop push button as an input to this system is used to stop the PLC system.\nThe purpose of the PLC unit as a process of this system, it will make a logical decision and give an instruction to the output field when necessary to turn the fan on or off.\nThe purpose of the relay as an output of this system it will be controlling the turning on or off of the fan motor\nSensors\nThis are non-contact switches that works on signals such as electro magnet, motion, light ect, the open or closes once they receive relevant signals also known as proximity sensors\nInductive, capacitive, reed switches and optical are four types of sensors each work on their specifications signals\nInductive sensor is used to detect metal objects\nMagnetic reed switch is used to detect the positions(extension and retraction of a cylinder)\nIt is activated by bringing a magnetic field into close proximity of the reed switch\nLimit switches or contact sensor can be used on gates\nOptical proximity sensors\nThree types are one-way system, reflection system & diffused reflection system\nOne-way system It makes use of independent transmitters and recieviers. The units which are mounted in a manner that are aligned up with each other. The output is automatically switched off when the light beam is broken . This method of saftey is effective with unskilled labour which can not by-pass these saftey devices\nReflective system cannot be used in a dirty environment, for small object detections, for objects reflecting light beams\nCapacitive sensor is used to detect any type of of objects without a contact by measuring the change in capacitance\nReacts to conductivity and non conductivity material by measuring the change in capacitance\nRelay ladder-logic hardwired control circuits are made up of event-based and time-based enabling conditions.\nEvent-based enabling conditions :detent switches, pushbuttons, sensors and relay contacts are combined to create an event.\nTimed-based enabling conditions :determined by timer relays\nThe timer is time based in that the preset time must elapse before any action can take place.\nCascaded timer-based control is achieved when all timers are activated at the same time but turn on/off at different times.\nDraw a fully labelled cascaded-control relay ladder-logic hardwired circuit with the correct terminal numbers using the symbols of the electrical elements, The system must be able to start and stop and THREE lamps must be turned on having 5-second intervals in a positive sequence after being started.\nThis is an example of cascaded timer based in a circuit\nActuators are used to link the control circuit to the working circuit in relay ladder logic hardwired mechatronic applications.\nThe difference in action between relay and solenoid valve-type actuators\nThe armature part of a relay is attached to contacts which are used to control electrical signals. The armature part of a solenoid valve is connected to a spool which controls the pressurised air.\nThe operation of the actuator solenoid\nis a coil which, when energised, becomes a magnet and attracts a moving part known as the armature.\nDepicts components which are difficult to draw; therefore, symbols that represent the components are used\nON/OFF detent switch\nMotor control relay\nIndication lamp\nDC moto\nDirect control\nIt can be achieved through detent switches to control loads such as lights as indicated below\nIndirect control\nIt is achieved via actuators such as relay which forms a bases of relay logic hardwire control\nA neat fully labelled drawing of a 24 V relay with a four changeover contact set arrangement. This is as you know the coil on those panel boxes\nThe changeover switch\nThe selected position is retained only for as long as it is actuated that when if the changeover operating with coil (relay above), or push detent button can be used if it is interconnected with both NO & NC contacts as one will always be close and one will always be opened irrespective of it position\nThe micro switch is a mechanical switch that is normally made up of a change over contact set that will be used to sense position by means of manual operation.\nThe difference between traffic light and robot\nTraffic light is an automatic signal controlling road traffic by combination of coloured lights\nRobot It is a reprogrammable , multifunctional manipulator designed to move materials, parts, tools or specialised devices through variable programmed motions for the performance of a variety of useful tasks.\nIt can be used to perfom various tasks such as arc welding, spot welding, material handling, machine tending, painting, picking, packing, palletising, assembling, cutting, grinding, pollishing\nComponents that learnt about in mechatronic systems that are used to generate a feedback signal on the status of a machine.\nIndication lamp\nHorn\nSiren\nBuzzer\nDial\nGauge\nIndication lamp is commonly used is commonly used to give status of the mechatronic system to the operator, RED: Emergency stop or On/Off GREEN: Start, On or Inching\nMechanical systems in mechatronics\nThe Pulley System\nAdvantages\nQuite in operation\nRequires no lubrication\nRelatively cheap to produce and simple in design (Any one)\nThe Chain System\nAdvantages\nPositive non-slip drive\nSimple in design (Any one)\nGear coupling\nAdvantages of a spur gear train transmission system\nCompactness\nMinimum backlash\n\n## 3. NC1000 - ELECTROTECHNOLOGY L2 MEMO NOV 2022 EDITED.pdf\n\nType: 