 and objective, aiming to present potential challenges associated with implementing this technology. ```\n\n## 2. NC2090 - MECHATRONIC SYSTEMS L2 QP SUPP 2019.pdf\n\nType: pdf | text chars: 5490 | page images: 15 | summary chars: 799\n\n### Summary\n\nThis document is a formal **examination paper** for a Level 2 mechatronics qualification, focusing on the fundamental principles of **mechanical and electrical engineering**. The assessment requires students to demonstrate their understanding of **energy conversion**, specifically by calculating work done and identifying kinetic or potential energy within industrial machinery. Significant emphasis is placed on **control systems**, tasking learners with explaining logic conditions and sketching **relay ladder-logic circuits** using standardized symbols for components like timers, sensors, and switches. Additionally, the text covers **pneumatic applications**, evaluating the student's ability to interpret technical diagrams and explain the internal mechanics of **solenoid-operated valves**.\n\n### Text\n\nMECHATRONIC SYSTEMS\nNQF LEVEL 2\n(6040102)\n12 March 2019 (X-Paper) 09:00–12:00\nThis question paper consists of 6 pages and 1 addendum.\nNATIONAL CERTIFICATE (VOCATIONAL)\n(6040102) -2- NC2090(E)(M12)V\nTIME: 3 HOURS\nMARKS: 100\nINSTRUCTIONS AND INFORMATION 1. 2. 3. 4. 5. 6. 7.\nAnswer ALL the questions. Read ALL the questions carefully. Number the answers according to the numbering system used in this question paper. ALL drawings must be neat and correctly labelled. ALL symbols must be of IEC standard. ALL terminal numbers must be labelled. Write neatly and legibly.\n(6040102) -3- NC2090(E)(M12)V\nQUESTION 1 1.1 Explain the term energy. (2) 1.2 List THREE sources of energy. (3) 1.3 The energy flow in technical systems can be represented by block diagrams\nthat show the energy conversion that takes place in a technical system, subsystem or components that make up the system. Draw a block diagram that represents energ