 assessment covers a diverse range of **core algebraic topics**, including number classifications, exponential laws, surds, financial formulas, and arithmetic sequences. To successfully complete the thirty-mark test, students must demonstrate their **problem-solving proficiency** and analytical abilities by applying mathematical rules without relying on shortcuts.\n\n### Text\n\nhigher education\n& training\nDepartment:\nHigher Education and Training REPUBLIC OF SOUTH AFRICA\nNAOWAJULU-NATAL\nPROVINCIAL GOVERNMENT\nKEN REGIONAL OFFICE\nNATIONAL CERTIFICATE (VOCATIONAL)\nFUNDAMENTALS MATHEMATICS NQF LEVEL 2\nTASK: 2(V1)\n1h30min Controlled\nDURATION: Environment\n18 MARCH 2026\nDATE:\nMARKS: 30\nICASS weighting: 10\nThis question paper consists of 6 pages including a formula sheet.\nSUBJECT OUTCOMES BEING ASSESSED:\nSUBJECT OUTCOMES\n\t\nLEARNING OUTCOMES\n\n1.1-1.2\n\t\n1.1.1-1.2.9\n1\nINSTRUCTIONS AND INFORMATION\n1.\nRead ALL the questions carefully.\n2.\n3.\n4.\n5.\n6\nAnswer ALL the questions.\nNumber the answers correctly according to the numbering system used in this question paper.\nWrite neatly and legibly.\nThe time allocated includes time for research and completion of the assignment. The Keying in/completion of the assignment must be done in controlled environment\nAll work you do not want to be marked must be clearly crossed out.\n2\nQUESTION 1\n1.1.\nVarious possible options are provided as answers to the following questions. Choose the correct answer and write only the letter $(A-D)$ next to the question number (1.1.1-1.1.5) in your ANSWER BOOK, for example 1.1.6 Α.\n1.1.1\n$\\sqrt{4}$ is\nA\n1.1.2\n1.1.3\nABCD\nThe square root of an irrational number A rational number and an irrational number A real and rational number Not a natural number\n$\\frac{2a^{-5}}{-3b^{2}}$\nA\nsimplified and in exponential form:\n$\\frac{2}{-3a^{5}b^{2}}$\nB $\\frac{2(3)}{a^{5}b^{2}}$\nC\n$\\frac{2a^{5}}{3b^{2}}$\nD\n$\\frac{7}{5}x^{\\frac{-5}{3}}$\n$\\frac{2(3)a^{5}}{b^{2}